course: dictionary
lesson: 11784
title: Beheaded: a word from history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Beheaded is the past form of the verb behead, which means to cut off someone's head. History books use it for serious events. «The king was beheaded, and the people in the story were shocked.» The word beheaded tells you what happened, and the clue is in the word itself: head.
explain: Beheaded can also describe things that have lost their top part, like a statue or a flower. «The statue in the park was beheaded in the storm, so only its body was left.» Its body is still there, but its head is gone, so beheaded means had the top part removed.
explain: Beheaded is a strong, serious word. When you read it, look at the words around it. Is the text about history or a serious event? If so, the word is describing something harsh. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «had its top part removed» still make sense? If yes, you have it.
fact: Beheaded means killed by having the head cut off.
fact: Beheaded can also mean having the head or top part removed, as with a flower or statue.
fact: Behead is the verb; beheaded is the past form, and beheading is the form used for the act itself.
fact: In history, kings and queens were beheaded, such as Anne Boleyn and Charles I in England.
fact: Beheaded is a serious word, so history uses it to show how harsh some punishments were.
exercise: «The gardener found the flower beheaded by the wind.» What does beheaded mean here? | Painted bright red | Watered every morning | Grown very tall | *Had its top part removed
exercise: Which word is the past form of the verb behead? | *beheaded | beheading | behead | beheads
exercise: In a history lesson, why is beheaded a serious word? | It describes a happy party | It is a word for a small pet | *It describes a violent death, so history uses it to show how harsh punishments were | It means very tired
test: «The old statue in the square had been beheaded, and only its shoulders remained.» What had happened to the statue? | It was painted gold | It grew a new head | It was moved to a new park | *Its head had been removed
test: Pick the word that means killed by having the head cut off. | *beheaded | rescued | captured | injured
exam: What does beheaded mean? | Lost in a crowd of people | *Killed by having the head cut off, or having the top part removed | Covered in snow | Very happy and full of joy
